## [:< ##

# name  = users.record.sorted_fields
# descr = which array-valued record fields get base.sort's canonical order
# param = -none-

## the single list, alongside users.record.default_fields' and
## .optional_fields' own vocabularies : per user, contact and phone both have
## no manual reorder control anywhere in the editor, so insertion order is
## arbitrary and reads as unintentional mess rather than a meaningful
## sequence.  three call sites read this rather than each naming the two
## fields for itself -- users.record.build [ normalises on every WRITE ],
## users.cmd.value-get [ normalises on every READ, read-only copy ], and
## user-edit.form.schema_from_record [ marks the field def so
## editor.control.list.expand normalises the moment focus ENTERS the list,
## mid-session, before either of the other two ever run ] -- the same "one
## implementation, not three, or they drift" reasoning
## editor.control.list.summary documents for itself.
##
## deliberately NOT "every array-valued field" : the vocabulary only has these
## two today, so the two forms are behaviourally identical right now, but
## naming them explicitly matches what was actually asked rather than
## committing every future list field to this by default.

return qw| contact phone |;

